-- title:
--   Local conjugacy of the commutant order away from r
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ and $\bar r$ be distinct primes, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $\{r,\bar r\}$, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring precisely when $r\in v$ or $\bar r\in v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and no strictly larger such submodule contains it. Let $c,d<0$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d]$ a division algebra locally exactly at the primes containing $r$, and $O$ a maximal order in it; similarly let $a_1,b_1<0$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$. Let $j:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map carrying $\Lambda$ into matrices with all entries in $O$, and $\tau:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map whose image is exactly the centraliser of $j(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule consisting precisely of those $x$ with all entries of $\tau(x)$ in $O$, let $\Lambda_1$ be any maximal order in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $r$. Then for every height-one prime $w\ne v$ there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ such that an element $x$ lies in the local box of $R$ at $w$ — the additive subgroup generated by the tensors $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$ — if and only if $x=uyu^{-1}$ for some $y$ in the local box of $\Lambda_1$ at $w$.
--
--   This is the statement that the order $R$ cut out in the definite quaternion algebra ramified at $\bar r$ by the centraliser of $j(\Lambda)$ inside $M_2(O)$ is, at every finite place other than the place above $r$, locally conjugate to an arbitrary maximal order; equivalently $R$ is maximal away from $r$. It feeds the construction of the Eichler order and the level structure on the fake elliptic curves used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of the Shimura curve.
